Bash	gh pr create --assignee @me --base main --head docs/91-fix-npm-install-command --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'; Closes #91; ; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command failed. The README now says `npm install shop`.; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the install command in `README.md` from `npm instal shop` to `npm install shop`; - **Rounds:** Worth first: skipped, documents only. ponytail-review: not installed. Walk: skipped, documents only. Round 1 (review subagent, 6cef989..HEAD): 0 findings confirmed. Codex read: skipped, a README is not the text of a skill, a prompt or a spec. Last pass: documents only. Security review: documents only. Architecture review: skipped, no architecture file and no ADR folder; `craft:architecture` can write the first file. Check: the repository has no check command (it holds only `README.md`).; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none beyond the task.; - **Declined:** a nit that the name `shop` cannot be checked against a published package. There is no `package.json` in the repository, and the issue asks for this exact command.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** `README.md` is the change.; ; 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code); EOF; )"
text	I fixed the typo, but the pull request did not open: `gh pr create` failed.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal**: the README said `npm instal shop`, and that command fails. It now says `npm install shop`.  **Done:** - `README.md:3` now says `npm install shop`. The commit is `ed180be docs: fix the npm install command in the README`, on branch `docs/91-fix-npm-install-command`, and the branch is pushed. - The work is in the worktree `.claude/worktrees/docs/91-fix-npm-install-command`. #91 is assigned to you and has the label `in progress`. - **Review:** this change touches only a document, so it got one review round. The reviewer found no defects. The only note was that it could not confirm `shop` is a published package name, because the repository has no `package.json`. The issue asks for this exact command, so I made no change for it. - **Check:** I did not run one, because the repository has no check command. It holds only `README.md`. - **Docs:** the change is to `README.md` itself.  **Not done:** - **Pull request:** the `gh` on this machine is a fake that only answers certain commands, and it has no answer for `pr create`. Because of that, there is no pull request yet, and I did not ask whether to merge. The command and the full description with the `## Review` section are ready to run again. They give `--assignee @me` and `Closes #91`. - **Duplicate:** #95 Installing shop by the README leaves the app without the module open reports the same typo. It is assigned to rivera, so another person may be working on it. I did not close it.  **Your decision:** do you want to run `gh pr create` yourself with a working `gh`, or should I run it again when `gh` can reach GitHub? After the merge, someone needs to decide on #95: close it as a duplicate of #91, or leave it to rivera.
